{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/175612-orange-is-the-new-black-uratha","id":175612,"title":"Orange is the New Black - Uratha","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-06-20T16:00:25-07:00","id":175612,"title":"Orange is the New Black - Uratha","content":"Anyone with a netflix subscription has probably been watching S2 of Orange is the new Black. I'm not incredibly fond but watch with my SO and boy did it give me some ideas for my Forsaken game. Not necessarily 'werewolves go to prison' but the whole tribal dynamic, and way some characters act. It just really made me think of werewolf. Oh and ah.. no spoilers for those who haven't watched the show. For example;<br /> <br /> Pennsatucky<br /> This chick is so clearly Fired-Touched. She's a mousy little thing but feisty, demands respect and leads her own little pack of followers. The rabid wolf is strong in this one. I've already written up a Fire-Touched Alpha based largely on her for a future story. And no the NPC is not named Pennsatucky. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> Red<br /> Edoloth Stormlord. She's alpha for one of the biggest packs in the prison. She says jump, you say 'how high? got it! While she's a strong Alpha she treats her pack with respect and dignity, so long as they can rise to her lofty standards.<br /> <br /> So what do you folks think? Does this show strike you as Forsaken? What other characters do you think would make a good Uratha?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1824-xaielao","name":"Xaielao","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1824_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"94"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-20T17:21:18-07:00","id":175645,"title":"","content":"I haven't seen Orange is the new Black, but I was a fan of Oz and believe I know what you mean.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-21T00:59:41-07:00","id":175855,"title":"","content":"It doesn't strike me as Forsaken, but I can see pack dynamics and can write characters as Uratha stereotypes, easily.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/137x125q90/745/a5GS5M.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/802-amaterasu","name":"amaterasu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"208"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}